prompt Take one bounded Systems Core lap, reds first, witness both sides, pull and send by xy.
think The cold roster ran 75 guards on tree digest ecd29d527ffd. Sixty-seven read GREEN and eight read RED. Caravan and Tally rosters were GREEN, and the full Caravan suite completed GREEN after its bounded ladder queue spent about twelve minutes. That delay was a machine cost, while the eight named evidence files were tree readings.
think Five reds shared one open-day synchronization drift chain: the day index cited a log absent from this clone, living-link reach failed on that row, the REDS fold inherited the broken reach, generated README metrics lagged, and the operator card named a deleted git nib in two guards. The second fetch showed the missing log had landed upstream while this lap ran. The rebase preserves that valid row, regenerates the metrics, and brings the nib to the commit seam.
think Two other roster reds are jail tool limits. equinox_e123_living_pin_guard_scan.sh and dated_pattern_scan.sh both reach their substantive verdict=ok, then fail when a planted control invokes rg, which this jail does not provide. Those are environment facts and no REDS row is booked.
think declared_ceiling remains the Mind-owned gated row %295. It names tools/l/chatgpt-mind.sh and the macOS-only SkateCore reach shape, so Dream records the reading and leaves that sibling lane whole. The REDS fold control itself passed 23 checks; its living reach leg failed only through the missing day log.
obs No other hand wrote this checkout before files moved. Sound and Silence appear in the newest handoff logs on their own clones; Sound repaired Dream's launcher, and Silence held a separate checkout during that repair. This grain-dream index was clean at open.
obs The first pull from xy failed before network contact because core.sshCommand names /home/keeper/grain/.git/ssh_config_urbit, absent inside this jail. HEAD and the last fetched xy/main both named c83e0ca25e. This is a pier configuration limit, not a tree defect.
obs The clone-local deploy key fetched xy through ssh with the system config disabled. Upstream moved three times during this lap. The first rebase supplied the missing 114450 log; later rebases carried newer logs and a newer ITINERARY row, which this lap preserved under the one-row card law.
obs Rota N=3606, N mod 5=1: Air and Saturn, law and boundary. The threshold, TAME Core, Single-Stranded, and Gauge say to press the edge. The absent log and floating nib were boundaries the hand passed through.
